; The one seam between the DUT-independent monitors and a live Hardcaml
; simulation (WO-0009's single sanctioned Axi64 import).
;
; It is a separate library, and not a module of dv_monitors, on purpose:
;
;  * dv_monitors and dv_golden then need no Hardcaml at all, so their tests
;    exercise monitor logic rather than an elaboration;
;  * SPEC-M01 §11.4 records that hardcaml_axi v0.17.0's Source field names are
;    unverified by any compile. This library is the first code to name them
;    (see axi64_probe.ml). If CI proves the transcription wrong, the failure is
;    confined to this directory and every other WO-0009 deliverable still
;    builds and runs.
;
; ifc_check is the lift of SPEC-M01 §4.1 under docs/specs/ — the signed public
; interface, byte-identical to the specification and countersigned at 22145b5.
; libs/** is not depended on and was not opened (PROTOCOL §10);
; libs/hardcaml_ethernet/src/axi64.ml does not exist at this SHA.

; hardcaml_step_testbench is deliberately NOT depended on here. It is in
; agentic_fpga.opam, so CI's `opam install --deps-only` already proves it
; resolves and installs — which was the request in WO-0003 findings §13.4. It
; is the framework for packet-level directed benches (charter §9) and the
; first of those arrives with M03, which has no frozen spec yet. Writing a
; step_testbench coroutine now, against an API no local build can check
; (ADR-0005), would put compile risk on this work order for no coverage. The
; monitors attach through a per-cycle closure (Protocol_monitor.sink), which a
; step_testbench cycle hook drives as readily as a Cyclesim loop, so nothing
; here has to change when that bench lands.

; WO-0033 added (inline_tests) and ppx_expect, which this library did not have
; at WO-0009. The reason is item X-6, the stream DRIVER: a sampler could only be
; tested against a live design, so there was nothing here to run; a driver can
; be tested against the sampler that already lives beside it, and
; drive-then-sample is exactly the round trip in which a wrong octet position
; is visible without any RTL. ppx_expect alone, not ppx_jane, matching
; test/monitors/dune — [%expect] is the only extension used.

(library
 (name dv_axi64_probe)
 (inline_tests)
 (libraries hardcaml hardcaml_axi ifc_check dv_monitors)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_expect)))
